# AI Model Extraction & Adversarial Distillation Research
**Independent Postgraduate Study** — May/June 2026

**Project Goal**: Simulate real-world adversarial attempts to steal training data or distill frontier model capabilities through large-scale prompt engineering.

This project demonstrates the exact proactive threat hunting and tooling development performed by Technical Threat Investigators at frontier AI companies like OpenAI.

### What I Built
- Custom Python prompt-fuzzing tool that runs entirely locally using Ollama
- 100+ intelligently mutated prompts designed to extract memorized training data
- Automated analysis and logging of model responses
- Full investigative workflow: seed → mutation → execution → documentation

### Tools & Environment
- Ollama + llama3.1:8b (local open-source model)
- Custom mutation logic for model extraction attacks

**Skills**:
- Adversarial thinking and proactive threat hunting
- Building investigative tooling and automation scripts
- Analyzing model behavior for memorization and extraction risks
- Documenting findings for technical and executive stakeholders

Full code, results, and analysis are in this folder.
